ness Survival, filed under Wilderness in the catalog, which the class also grants. Science: none, so it is not offered. || SECONDARY: three at each of levels one, five and ten, from the same list without bonuses; the book says select three at levels one, five and ten, read as three per level as the book''s other classes print it. || MONEY: one month''s salary, 2500 credits; room and board are free. || EQUIPMENT: Kuru or Trooper armor is a choice of the AT-A11 Kuru Street Armor and the AT-A14 Trooper rows. Energy rifle and sidearm of choice are offered from this book''s ArmaTech and H-Brand sets, with four E-clips each. The AT-D30 stun/flash grenade (printed 130) has no catalog row, so the generic stun/flash grenade row stands in, beside the AT-D31 tear gas grenade. The survival kit is stored as its listed contents. Two non-energy weapons of choice are offered from this book''s vibro-blades, swords, tonfa and rail guns. || POWER ARMOR: the SAMAS itself (ArmaTech Samurai Class SAMAS, printed 132-135) is not in the catalog yet; it is described in the Issued Power Armor section and side_effects, to be wired to the vehicles tables once the book''s power armor is imported. Upon Special Assignment (SNARLS sensor system, AT-ADD grenades, heavy weapons) is situational and is in GM Notes."
